# Security And No-Claim Proof

No-claim boundaries preserved:

- Inventory evidence is rejected before journal append if it claims runtime,
  foreground, running duration, or foreground duration.
- Runtime evidence is rejected before journal append if it claims foreground
  state.
- Foreground evidence is rejected unless it is foreground-window evidence with
  `contentKnowledgeState = notClaimed`.
- Launcher evidence cannot be promoted to known-game proof without a child-game
  evidence claim.
- Launcher-only evidence stays launcher-only.
- Permission-limited launcher classification must carry permission-limited
  capability state.
- AI output cannot enforce; no AI path changed.
- Manual-required states cannot execute adapters; no adapter path changed.
- Raw private executable paths remain evidence refs in fixture rows and no UI
  path was added.
- Duplicate runtime observations do not double count duration after replay.

Validation coverage:

```text
cargo test -p ocentra-parent-agent-core app_game_journal_sqlite -- --nocapture
PASS: invalid evidence rejection, duplicate-duration guard, and replay read model.

cargo test -p ocentra-parent-agent-core app_game -- --nocapture
PASS: existing app/game no-claim and sessionization coverage stayed green.
```
